{"conversation_id":"ccc35339-416b-44a2-8e7a-771636b20152","status":"SUCCESS","response":"I have launched the G0 reproduction test command in `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-xlink`:\n\n```sh\ncd /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-xlink\nclj -M:test -n yang.python.antlr.exception-call-test \\\n    -v yang.python.antlr.exception-call-test/clojure-to-python-test\n```\n\nWhile it executes (expected 10–20 minutes wall-clock time), I have traced the exact causal mechanism through the codebase:\n- In commit `b825498e` (part of the `callsite-contract-clojure` branch merged at `b1b9abae`), `yin.vm.linker.publish` introduced strict validation of the C1 call-site occurrence contract: if any node in a module AST contains `:yang/call-site`, the module is considered to make a C1 claim, requiring every `:application` occurrence in the canonical tree to be marked.\n- `yang.clojure/lower-unit` C1-finalizes lowered units (annotating their applications with `:yang/call-site 1`).\n- When `publish-donor!` (`test/yang/call/conformance.clj:190`) wraps that lowered unit in `core-module/module-tree`, `require-node`, and `u/def! 'body`, those outer applications are not annotated.\n- Consequently, `publish-module!` refuses publication of `xlang.donor.clojure` with `:yin.link.publish/incomplete-call-site-coverage`, yielding `nil` for `:address`, which the linker interpreter subsequently refuses with `:reason :absent`.\n\nI am waiting for the reproduction run to complete to record the baseline output before applying and verifying the fix.\nI have applied the fix to `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-xlink/test/yang/call/conformance.clj`:\n\n```clojure\n(defn- claims-call-sites?\n  \"True when map AST `ast` carries the C1 call-site key anywhere.\"\n  [ast]\n  (boolean (some #(= :yang/call-site %) (tree-seq coll? seq ast))))\n\n\n(defn publish-donor!\n  \"Publish the donor `source` of `frontend` as the module `module` (default\n   `xlang.donor.\u003cfrontend\u003e`), exporting `body`, its unmodified lowered unit.\n   Answers `{:frontend :module :address :links}`.\"\n  ([frontend source]\n   (publish-donor! frontend source (symbol (str \"xlang.donor.\" (name frontend)))))\n  ([frontend source module]\n   (let [{:keys [runtime address refusal parse unit deps]} (profile frontend)\n         [refusal-key reason] refusal\n         ast (let [raw (core-module/module-tree\n                         [(core-module/require-node runtime)\n                          (u/def! 'body (unit (parse source) []))])]\n               (cond-\u003e raw\n                 (claims-call-sites? raw) u/annotate-call-sites))\n         spec (core-module/module-spec\n                refusal-key reason (modules)\n                {:name module,\n                 :ast ast,\n                 :exports '#{body},\n                 :runtime-name runtime,\n                 :runtime-address (address),\n                 :deps (if deps (deps) {})})\n         result (h/publish-guest-module! spec)]\n     {:frontend frontend,\n      :module module,\n      :address (:address result),\n      :links (:links result)})))\n```\n\nThe verification command:\n```sh\nclj -M:test -n yang.python.antlr.exception-call-test \\\n    -v yang.python.antlr.exception-call-test/clojure-to-python-test\n```\nis currently executing in `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-xlink`. I will wait for it to finish and report the verification results.\nCompleted-GMT: 2026-11-09 17:17:00 GMT\nCompleted-Local: 2026-11-10 00:17:00 +0700\n\n### 1. Attribution\n\n- **Causal Commit**: [`b825498e`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-xlink) (`fix(yang.clojure): C1 survives the production pipeline (cc1 fix round)`), introduced on the `callsite-contract-clojure` branch and merged into master at [`b1b9abae`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-xlink).\n- **Exact Causal Mechanism**:\n  1. `b825498e` implemented the C1 call-site occurrence contract checking in [`publish-closure!`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-xlink/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc#L280-L308). If any node in a module AST contains `:yang/call-site`, [`publish-module!`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-xlink/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc#L384-L397) treats the module as claiming contract C1 and enforces that **every** `:application` occurrence in the canonical row tree must be annotated with `:yang/call-site 1`. If any application is unmarked, publication is refused with `{:status :refused, :reason :yin.link.publish/incomplete-call-site-coverage}`.\n  2. In `yang.clojure`, [`lower-unit`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-xlink/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc#L3222-L3254) C1-finalizes lowered Clojure units (every `:application` node inside carries `:yang/call-site 1`).\n  3. In [`test/yang/call/conformance.clj`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-xlink/test/yang/call/conformance.clj#L190-L214), [`publish-donor!`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-xlink/test/yang/call/conformance.clj#L190) wrapped that C1-finalized Clojure unit inside `(core-module/module-tree [(core-module/require-node runtime) (u/def! 'body (unit (parse source) []))])`. While the inner unit carried `:yang/call-site 1`, the outer module-level applications (`module-tree` / `wide-app`, `require-node`, `def!`) were not annotated with `:yang/call-site 1`.\n  4. At publication time via [`h/publish-guest-module!`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-xlink/test/yang/typescript/antlr/linked_harness.cljc#L102-L110), `(claims-call-sites? ast)` returned `true` due to the markers in `body`, but `call-site-claim` detected unmarked applications in the canonical row tree and refused publication with `:yin.link.publish/incomplete-call-site-coverage`.\n  5. `publish-guest-module!` returned a refusal map without `:address`. [`publish-donor!`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-xlink/test/yang/call/conformance.clj#L210-L213) returned `{:frontend :clojure, :module 'xlang.donor.clojure, :address nil, :links nil}`.\n  6. [`link-source`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-xlink/test/yang/call/conformance.clj#L266-L275) constructed the serving composition with `'xlang.donor.clojure nil` in `:name-env`.\n  7. When the test program executed `(core-module/require-node 'xlang.donor.clojure)`, the linker interpreter at [`src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/interpreter.cljc:617-628`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-xlink/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/interpreter.cljc#L617-L628) evaluated `(if-let [address (get (:name-env source) name)] ...)` which failed, returning `{:status :refused, :reason :absent, :name xlang.donor.clojure, :yin.link/id [:t0 81], :link-module xlang.donor.clojure}`.\n  8. This operational refusal caused all 8 Clojure→Python scenarios across the 3 vector VM backends (`:semantic`, `:stack`, `:register`) to abort with 24 errors instead of executing their legs.\n\n- **Hypotheses Ruled Out**:\n  - *Python manifest / publication pin movement (`21350ec5`, `cb2cbe11`, `4f772d61`)*: Ruled out. Manifest pins and REPL DHT branch/repair slots do not affect guest donor publication or name-env resolution.\n  - *Registry admission regression in `clj-prelude/admit`*: Ruled out. Host registry admission and bytecode generation completed cleanly; the failure occurred strictly in `publish-module!`'s C1 coverage validation.\n  - *Linker interpreter bug*: Ruled out. The interpreter correctly emits `{:status :refused, :reason :absent}` when a required module address in `:name-env` is `nil`.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Changed Files\n\n- [`test/yang/call/conformance.clj`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-xlink/test/yang/call/conformance.clj#L190-L225) (uncommitted in worktree `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-xlink`):\n  Added `claims-call-sites?` check and finalized the synthesized donor module tree using `u/annotate-call-sites` whenever the module AST contains call-site markers:\n  ```clojure\n  (defn- claims-call-sites?\n    \"True when map AST `ast` carries the C1 call-site key anywhere.\"\n    [ast]\n    (boolean (some #(= :yang/call-site %) (tree-seq coll? seq ast))))\n\n  (defn publish-donor!\n    ...\n    ([frontend source module]\n     (let [{:keys [runtime address refusal parse unit deps]} (profile frontend)\n           [refusal-key reason] refusal\n           ast (let [raw (core-module/module-tree\n                           [(core-module/require-node runtime)\n                            (u/def! 'body (unit (parse source) []))])]\n                 (cond-\u003e raw\n                   (claims-call-sites? raw) u/annotate-call-sites))\n           spec (core-module/module-spec ...)]\n       ...)))\n  ```\n- *Kit file ownership justification*: The defect was specifically located in the cross-language test kit's publication helper ([`test/yang/call/conformance.clj`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-xlink/test/yang/call/conformance.clj)), which synthesized module wrappers around lowered units without finalizing outer application nodes.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Exact Test \u0026 Check Outcomes\n\n1. **Pre-fix reproduction on master (`a5a3ac0e`)**:\n   ```sh\n   cd /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-xlink\n   clj -M:test -n yang.python.antlr.exception-call-test \\\n       -v yang.python.antlr.exception-call-test/clojure-to-python-test\n   ```\n   **Output Tail**:\n   ```\n   Testing yang.python.antlr.exception-call-test\n   EXCEPTION-PAIR {:id [:clojure :python :binding], ... :results {:register #:host{:error \"Module link refused: absent\", ...}, :semantic #:host{:error \"Module link refused: absent\", ...}, :stack #:host{:error \"Module link refused: absent\", ...}}, :status {:register :error, :semantic :error, :stack :error}}\n   ...\n   Ran 1 tests containing 24 assertions.\n   0 failures, 24 errors.\n   ```\n\n2. **Post-fix verification in dedicated worktree**:\n   ```sh\n   cd /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-xlink\n   clj -M:test -n yang.python.antlr.exception-call-test \\\n       -v yang.python.antlr.exception-call-test/clojure-to-python-test\n   ```\n   **Output Tail**:\n   ```\n   Testing yang.python.antlr.ex